1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
FOUR ROBOTS. TWO JUMPERS.
A close look at cooperative rope skipping in MuJoCo.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:28,000
ONE COMPLETE PHYSICAL RUN
Startup is included. Scoring begins after simulation time 9 seconds.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:48,000
01 / THE LEFT MOUTH CONNECTION
The rope follows a mouth-held handle driven by the robot.

4
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:08,000
02 / THE RIGHT MOUTH CONNECTION
Both ends are physically attached. No motion-capture carriers.

5
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:32,000
03 / SKY: TAKEOFF, CLEARANCE, LANDING
Orange is the rope; the dark line on the floor is its shadow.

6
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:56,000
04 / GRAPHITE: WATCH BOTH SOLES
A clean cycle requires sole clearance and a supported landing.

7
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:16,000
05 / TWO ROBOTS, THE SAME ROPE
Both jumpers must pass the same full cycle for it to count.

8
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:32,000
06 / SPACE FOR EVERY ROBOT
Turner spacing 0.80 m  |  Rope 0.86 m  |  Jumper spacing 0.28 m

9
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:56,000
07 / MOVING ENTRY: STILL UNSOLVED
This attempt touches the rope during entry and is graded FAIL.

10
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:08,000
08 / WHY ENTRY FAILS: JAW CONTACT
The rope touches the lower jaw at 15.595s. Red dots mark geometric contact.

11
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:20,000
258 / 260 SHARED CLEAN CYCLES
Four independent 30-second static-duo runs; first 9s excluded in each.
